(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The dispatch loop (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): one loop per entry from Go, running frames until"] [4 1 "// the entry frame returns. A call of a Python function pushes its frame and continues; a return pops"] [5 1 "// it. An exception unwinds by the exception table: the covering handler's depth, lasti and target,"] [6 1 "// else the frame is left and the caller's instruction raises it."] [8 1 "// guardedStep is step with a Go panic of the runtime turned into a SystemError raised at f's instruction"] [9 1 "// (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core, PY6a's Low: a panic ended the whole lib-test module, now only its test)"] [14 31 "// the C-level checks' increments the panic skipped"] [15 31 "// and a direct call's (queue 216d), had the panic crossed one"] [20 3 "// step's own frame not entered for compiled code (queue 216d); while tracing, the loop (queue 219t): a compiled"] [21 3 "// frame hands itself over at a block start (AotToLoop)"] [29 1 "// run runs f (and the frames it calls) to f's return: Go's call into the machine, CPython's"] [30 1 "// _PyEval_EvalFrameDefault entered from C, the C level's recursion check first (where \"\", PY7)."] [41 1 "// runFrames is run's loop, f its entry frame. direct (queue 216d): f is a callee a compiled caller runs from its own Go"] [42 1 "// code (callDirect) where it would have returned f as its *pushFrame: f entered as this loop enters a pushed frame,"] [43 1 "// the eval breaker's error raised in f, and no C level counted (a Python call is none: run's check is Go's entry)."] [47 18 "// f_back of an escaped frame reaches its callers (202b)"] [55 31 "// a direct callee's RESUME error, raised in it as in a pushed frame"] [56 31 "// RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go)"] [65 41 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW (queue 220; breakMonitor)"] [78 37 "// PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD (queue 220): a callback's error raised in f"] [82 5 "// a jump (f_lineno) from the yield's event: the frame goes on there, the value not yielded"] [83 5 "// (INSTRUMENTED_YIELD_VALUE's frame->instr_ptr check; queue 281: test_sys_settrace's test_jump_from_yield)"] [89 4 "// f returned v"] [97 21 "// a suspended generator's f_back is None (its caller may be reused: releaseFrame)"] [105 5 "// callInit's __init__ returned: the instance is the call's value (type_call's check of __init__'s)"] [118 4 "// a call of a Python function from f: run the callee in this loop"] [133 5 "// the callee's RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go), its error raised in the callee; then"] [134 5 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START (queue 220: breakMonitor keeps the breaker set while a tool has events)"] [145 3 "// an exception in f at f.Lasti"] [151 4 "// an exception the runtime raised in f (a KeyError of d[k] ...): chained as _PyErr_SetObject chains"] [156 40 "// a re-raise adds no entry for the frame it is raised in (exception_unwind)"] [157 40 "// RERAISE (queue 281: monitor_reraise)"] [165 41 "// END_ASYNC_FOR's RERAISE (queue 281)"] [168 45 "// RAISE (queue 219t): settrace's 'exception'"] [173 43 "// EXCEPTION_HANDLED (queue 281: monitor_handled)"] [183 47 "// frame->instr_ptr: a reraise N's restored instruction"] [189 24 "// PY_UNWIND (queue 220)"] [191 6 "// the handler CPython wraps a generator's body in (codegen's STOPITERATION_ERROR and RERAISE; queue 281)"] [207 1 "// OpImpl implements an operation outside step's switch (PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): it pops and pushes f's"] [208 1 "// stack itself and returns (nil, nil) to go on; (nil, err) raises; (nil, *pushFrame) runs a Python"] [209 1 "// function's frame next; (v, nil) makes f return v (a generator's yield sets f.Suspended first)."] [212 1 "// opImpls are the operations registered by the files that own them (§9), each by its file's init:"] [213 1 "// RegisterOp(OpLoadAttr, ...). An operation of step's switch is never looked up here."] [216 1 "// RegisterOp sets op's implementation; a second one is a programming error (one owner per operation)."] [224 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [227 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [228 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [229 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [230 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [234 22 "// sys.monitoring's CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [246 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [259 4 "// a built-in method bound to its object (BuiltinType's call slot): its arguments made at once with self"] [260 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [276 51 "// next(gen()): the generator dies at the return (queue 297)"] [299 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [308 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [309 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [310 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [313 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [314 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect: its value pushed on f's stack, or its exception returned); else returned"] [315 1 "// as the thread's *pushFrame, read by runFrames before the thread's next call."] [324 1 "// callDirect runs callee, a compiled function's frame called by f's compiled code (queue 216d, the user's (a) on"] [325 1 "// 216's DECISION 1): a loop of it